From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?S=C3=A9bastien=20Celles?= <s.celles@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 7 Jun 2026 13:28:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 46/62] verimark: send 0x96 03 commit on the IT with minimal
 1-byte payload
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The previous skip-commit hypothesis was disproved by the
RESOLVE_TUID diag log : pre_count == post_count == 8 on the IT,
meaning the template was never persisted. The 0x96 03 commit is
needed to write the RAM working slot to NVRAM ; without it the
template only lives in firmware RAM until 0x96 04 finish clears
it.

The DT 123-byte commit payload (TUID + SID + footer) was the
trigger of the original 0x0404 BAD_STATE on the IT. The IT
likely expects a different / shorter payload. As the smallest
hypothesis : send just the sub-command byte 0x03 with no body
and inspect the firmware response in enr_cb_commit.

If 0x0000 → template persisted, getlist will show count+1 ; if
0x0404 or another status, log it and grow the payload structure
based on the firmware's response.
---
 libfprint/drivers/verimark/verimark.c | 29 ++++++++++++++++++---------
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libfprint/drivers/verimark/verimark.c b/libfprint/drivers/verimark/verimark.c
index c9dc34a..966153d 100644
--- a/libfprint/drivers/verimark/verimark.c
+++ b/libfprint/drivers/verimark/verimark.c
@@ -2571,16 +2571,27 @@ enroll_sm_run_state(FpiSsm *ssm, FpDevice *dev)
         fpi_ssm_next_state(ssm);
         return;
     case ENR_S_COMMIT_CALL: {
-        /* IT firmware auto-commits when it signals enroll-complete via
-         * 0x8006 on add_image. Sending the DT-style 0x96 03 commit on
-         * the IT is rejected with VERIMARK_STATUS_BAD_STATE (0x0404)
-         * because the firmware is already in idle state. Skip to
-         * DB_REFRESH so the new TUID is still resolved via the pre/post
-         * getlist diff (same as the DT post-commit path). */
+        /* IT : the previous "skip 0x96 03" hypothesis was wrong — the
+         * RESOLVE_TUID diag log showed pre_count == post_count after
+         * IT enroll, meaning the template was NEVER persisted to NVRAM.
+         * The 0x96 03 commit IS required to write the RAM working slot
+         * to NVRAM. The DT 123-byte commit payload is rejected on the
+         * IT with 0x0404 (BAD_STATE) ; the IT seems to expect either
+         * no payload or a different structure. Send an empty payload as
+         * the simplest hypothesis. */
         GUsbDevice *usb = fpi_device_get_usb_device(dev);
-        if (usb != NULL && g_usb_device_get_pid(usb) == VERIMARK_PID_IT) {
-            fp_info("verimark: IT enroll skipping 0x96 03 (firmware auto-commits)");
-            fpi_ssm_next_state(ssm);
+        const gboolean is_it = (usb != NULL &&
+                                g_usb_device_get_pid(usb) == VERIMARK_PID_IT);
+        if (is_it) {
+            /* Minimal payload : just the sub-command byte 0x03 = commit.
+             * The DT's 123-byte body (TUID + SID + footer) was rejected
+             * with 0x0404 on the IT. Try the smallest valid framing
+             * first ; we can grow it incrementally if needed. */
+            static const uint8_t it_commit_payload[1] = { 0x03 };
+            fp_warn("verimark: IT enroll sending 0x96 03 with 1-byte payload");
+            verimark_session_call_opcode_async(&self->session, self->transport,
+                3000, 0x96, it_commit_payload, sizeof(it_commit_payload),
+                cancel, enr_cb_commit, ssm);
             return;
         }
         uint8_t commit_payload[123];
